":"Coop Prix Byhaven","g":"essentials","k":"supermarket","la":58.148182,"lo":7.990354,"d":576,"h":"Mo-Fr 07:00-22:00, Sa 07:00-20:00","w":"https://www.coop.no/butikker/coop-prix/coop-prix-byhaven-2716","ph":"+47 90 77 14 00"},{"n":"Kilden Teater","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":58.142864,"lo":7.995264,"d":309,"ds":"Kilden Teater is a Norwegian theatre based in Kristiansand. It was established in 1991, and has been the regional theatre for Agder since 1995. It was earlier named Agder Teater, but changed its name after moving in to the new Kilden Performing Arts Centre.","wpu":"Kilden Teater","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Kilden-Kristiansand.JPG/960px-Kilden-Kristiansand.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Lagmannsholmen","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":58.1399,"lo":7.9917,"d":358,"ds":"Lagmannsholmen is a former island in Kristiansand Municipality in Agder county, Norway. It sits at the entrance to the western part of the harbor of the town of Kristiansand, just northwest of the island of Odderøya. Starting in 1686, the island was the site of the fleet station for the Danish-Norwegian galley fleet (Skjærbåt).","wpu":"Lagmannsholmen","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Christiansand034.jpg/960px-Christiansand034.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Fiskebrygga, Kristiansand","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":58.140833,"lo":7.995833,"d":418,"ds":"Fiskebrygga (English: The Fish Wharf) is a former fish landing in the city of Kristiansand in Agder county, Norway. The buildings have been redeveloped as a restaurant, shopping area, and tourist destination. The former fish landing extends along both sides of Gravane Canal, the canal that separates the town centre, Kvadraturen, from the island of Odderøya.","wpu":"Fiskebrygga, Kristiansand","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Kristiansand%2C_Norway_-_panoramio_%286%29.jpg/960px-Kristiansand%2C_Norway_-_panoramio_%286%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"St. Ansgar's Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":58.14469,"lo":7.99775,"d":492,"ds":"St. Ansgar's Church is a parish church of the Roman Catholic Church in the town of Kristiansand in Kristiansand Municipality in Agder county, Norway. It is the only Roman Catholic church building in Agder county in Southern Norway.","wpu":"St. Ansgar's Church","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f6/St._Ansgar_katolske_krk._Krsand.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Kilden Performing Arts Centre","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":58.139114,"lo":7.997147,"d":602,"ds":"Kilden Performing Arts Centre (in Norwegian: Kilden teater og konserthus) is a theater and concert hall on Odderøya in Kristiansand, Norway. It houses Kilden Teater, Kristiansand Symphony Orchestra (KSO), Kilden Opera and Kilden Culture Venue in a joint project never previously embarked upon. There is room for a variety of concerts and other forms of cultural expression.","wpu":"Kilden Performing Arts Centre","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Kilden%2C_Kristiansand%2C_Vest-Agder%2C_Norway_-_panoramio_%281%29.jpg/960px-Kilden%2C_Kristiansand%2C_Vest-Agder%2C_Norway_-_panoramio_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Grim Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":58.148,"lo":7.9724,"d":1172,"ds":"Grim Church (Norwegian: Grim kirke) is a parish church of the Church of Norway in Kristiansand Municipality in Agder county, Norway. It is located in the borough of Grim in the city of Kristiansand, just northwest of the city centre. It is the church for the Grim parish which is part of the Kristiansand domprosti (arch-deanery) in the Diocese of Agder og Telemark.","wpu":"Grim Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Grim_kirke_II.jpg/960px-Grim_kirke_II.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Odderøya","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":58.13534,"lo":8.00415,"d":1189,"ds":"Odderøya is an island in Kristiansand Municipality in Agder county, Norway. The 0.7-square-kilometre (170-acre) island lies immediately to the south of the city centre of Kristiansand and it is connected to the mainland by four bridges. The island creates a natural division between the eastern and western parts of the port of Kristiansand.","wpu":"Odderøya","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Gravanekanalen_16.jpg/960px-Gravanekanalen_16.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Baneheia","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":58.15367,"lo":7.98586,"d":1211,"ds":"Baneheia is a recreational area in Kristiansand Municipality in Agder county, Norway. The park is mostly known at the national level from the Baneheia case as the scene of a notorious murder of two girls ages 8 and 10 that took place in 2000. The area lies just north of the centre of the city of Kristiansand and it has hills, lakes, and forest.","wpu":"Baneheia","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/3._stampe.JPG/960px-3._stampe.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Lund Church (Agder)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":58.1526,"lo":8.0121,"d":1679,"ds":"Lund Church (Norwegian: Lund kirke) is a parish church of the Church of Norway in Kristiansand Municipality in Agder county, Norway. It is located in the district of Lund in the borough of Lund near the central part of the city of Kristiansand. It is the church for the Lund parish which is part of the Kristiansand domprosti (arch-deanery) in the Diocese of Agder og Telemark.","wpu":"Lund Church (Agder)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Lund_kyrkje_i_Kristiansand.jpg/960px-Lund_kyrkje_i_Kristiansand.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Ravnedalen, Kristiansand","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":58.155603,"lo":7.973113,"d":1716,"ds":"Ravnedalen is a park in Kristiansand Municipality in Agder county, Norway. The part is located in the borough of Grim, north of the centre of the city of Kristiansand, just to the northeast of the Baneheia recreation area. The park was constructed from 1874–1878 by military soldiers under the command of Colonel, later Major General, Joseph Frantz Oscar Wergeland.","wpu":"Ravnedalen, Kristiansand","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Ravnedalen_Kristiansand.jpg/960px-Ravnedalen_Kristiansand.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Oddernes stone","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":58.159444,"lo":8.013333,"d":2284,"ds":"The Oddernes stone (Oddernessteinen) is a rune stone from Oddernes Church at Oddernes in Kristiansand, Vest-Agder, Norway. The stone was originally just in the church yard east of the church. In 1990 it was moved into the church porch.","wpu":"Oddernes stone","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Oddernessteinen-SNL.jpg/960px-Oddernessteinen-SNL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Diocese of Agder og Telemark","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":58.1667,"lo":8,"d":2699,"ds":"The Diocese of Agder og Telemark (Norwegian: Agder og Telemark bispedømme) is a diocese of the Church of Norway, covering all of Agder county and Telemark county in Norway. The cathedral city is Kristiansand, Norway's fifth largest city. Kristiansand Cathedral serves as the seat of the presiding Bishop.","wpu":"Diocese of Agder og Telemark","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Bisped%C3%B8mmer_i_Norge.svg/960px-Bisped%C3%B8mmer_i_Norge.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Bragdøya","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":58.11862,"lo":7.99259,"d":2715,"ds":"Bragdøya is an uninhabited island in Kristiansand Municipality in Agder county, Norway. The 0.7-square-kilometre (0.27 sq mi) island is in the archipelago in the Kristiansandsfjorden, just south of the city of Kristiansand. The island is surrounded by the smaller islands of Svensholmen and Langøya to the north (across the narrow Bragdøyrenna strait) and the island of Hestehaue to the southeast.","wpu":"Bragdøya","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Bragd%C3%B8ya_IMG_3162_kjosbukta.JPG/960px-Bragd%C3%B8ya_IMG_3162_kjosbukta.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Kristiansand (Norwegian pronunciation: [ˈkrɪstɪansan] ) is a city located within Kristiansand Municipality in Agder county, Norway. The city is the administrative centre of both Kristiansand Municipality and Agder county. The city sits along the southern coast of Norway, along the Skagerrak.","wpu":"Kristiansand","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a5/Kvadraturen-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}